  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c0b1a6-2957-4d83-b47d-64c8c8f2bbc0"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the formal variable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[HBar]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f7a9013-f612-4487-81f1-dd43991ac0b1"],
 " of the Beilinson-Drinfeld algebra.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0f1ab530-e4bb-4b30-a156-2f8af18fd4cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HBar"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HBar", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0cbc3f29-8b73-4280-9a52-acb00552eb65"],
 " is a symbol with no value."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - HBar is an ordinary symbol with no value, by \
design the one export of the paclet that carries none; it was the engine's \
hbar until T0b. Every operation treats it as a scalar through the scalar \
tests of its linearity rules, and it has even degree, so it never enters a \
Koszul sign. Its degree is given by ElementDegree in the symmetric grading \
only, 2(n - 3), the degree that makes the operator homogeneous of degree -1; \
in the other two gradings it returns unevaluated, a decision of R5f kept by \
Pavel. The verification suites load their engine after the paclet, so the \
engine's HBar is this symbol. Prior art: in the Wolfram Language the \
character \\[HBar] is a letter that makes an ordinary symbol of the current \
context, with no built-in meaning.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->772555111,ExpressionUUID->"72606f13-3b64-4726-a725-0490e4c8e4e6"],

Cell["Every operation treats it as a scalar.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"86add2b2-2552-4772-82d5-63c6f67714a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its symmetric degree is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["ElementDegree"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/ElementDegree", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"HBar", ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Symmetric\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c2055eb-d5f2-42a7-a016-2d8d9a694cba"],
 ", which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "3"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e46c31b-cebb-4aa1-8e0e-68de41672efb"],
 ". It has no bar or exterior degree."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2d3ad333-f40d-48a4-9c4e-4e4b802366dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is the weight of the bracket term in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalBeilinsonDrinfeldOperator"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalBeilinsonDrinfeldOperator", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e94f4070-8d8d-43c7-a38b-21eca9dd2510"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "^"], 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "^"], 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "0"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " "}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["q", "TI"], "^"], 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8c0d0c4-00dc-4214-8681-a77cf861b5bd"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ffda2cc4-370d-4deb-bdeb-00c97ae7bfe5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In a BD action it is the weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6358fc7f-f6cb-4d3b-9596-bc77a3542443"],
 " of the genus-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f9e0b41-1208-4f1e-88f8-34a4c9ff1297"],
 " component."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8f30a37f-ef6f-43ab-b4ff-4dd9d77a6a55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The BD formalism never inverts it. Negative powers appear only in the \
localized BV picture, where the BV action is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8c13c16-b800-4736-b475-e7f36d28c199"],
 " times the BD one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3993670d-74c0-4699-befe-9d80eb382b76"],

